invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_host
reason: ch_srv_check stops asking for the caller's description of its
  CPU, so a boot check passes a configuration every server init call
  refuses. test/tcp_blocking_loop_cpu.h requires ch_srv_check to refuse
  the values the init calls refuse.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    // Every init call refuses this description of the CPU, so the check
    // refuses it too, before either identity signs.
    if (!cpu_bits_ok(cfg)) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
#endif
--- new
